use flake

# Keep compiled fasls inside the project.
#
# ASDF defaults to ~/.cache/common-lisp, which is outside the workspace and not
# writable from a sandboxed shell -- so any SBCL invocation that had to compile
# something (rather than reuse a warm cache) died on "Can't create directory".
# Redirecting output translations fixes it for every entry point at once: mise
# tasks, run-tests.sh, and bare `sbcl --script` on the experiment scripts.
#
# Scoped to ASDF deliberately. Setting XDG_CACHE_HOME would work too but would
# also redirect every other tool's cache for anything run in this directory.
export ASDF_OUTPUT_TRANSLATIONS="/:$PWD/tmp/fasl/"
mkdir -p "$PWD/tmp/fasl"
